20. FORMULAS AND BUSINESS RULES

Implement these rules consistently across the application.

A. Q-Matic processing percentage:

If Q-Matic Issued > 0:

Processed on OneApp / Q-Matic Issued × 100.

If both values are zero, display N/A.

If processed exceeds issued, flag an inconsistency.

B. OneApp reconciliation percentage:

If OneApp TIDs Issued > 0:

(Processed OneApp + Skipped OneApp TIDs) / OneApp TIDs Issued × 100.

If all three values are zero, display N/A.

If processed plus skipped exceeds issued, flag an inconsistency.

C. Remaining OneApp TIDs:

Issued − Processed − Skipped.

If this is positive, display the number of unaccounted TIDs.

If negative, flag a discrepancy.

D. Zone-level percentages:

Calculate percentages using the sum of the relevant counts across reporting offices.

Never calculate the zone-wide percentage by averaging individual office percentages.

E. Office coverage:

Reporting office coverage = Offices with valid confirmed reports / Active offices expected to report × 100.

Display missing reports separately. Never treat missing reports as zero-activity reports.

F. Approved OneApp and Pak-ID totals:

Sum the corresponding approved, deferred, and correction quantities from validated records. Do not infer one status from another.

G. Daily and historical data:

All calculations must use the selected date or date range, with no unintended mixing of reporting periods.

