* Complete frontend source code.
* Complete backend source code.
* Database schema and migrations.
* Sample seed data clearly marked as demo data.
* OCR processing implementation and configuration.
* Environment-variable example file without real secrets.
* Authentication and permissions implementation.
* API documentation.
* Automated tests.
* Production build configuration.
* Installation instructions.
* Deployment instructions.
* Backup and recovery instructions.
* Troubleshooting guide.

Do not return only a design, mockup, landing page, or sample dashboard.

Do not leave essential functions as non-working buttons or simulated success messages.

If an external OCR provider or service is required, document its setup and limitations explicitly. Do not claim image recognition is working until the actual processing pipeline has been implemented and tested.

Begin by designing the database and application architecture, then implement the complete application with a polished UI, functional dashboards, image-to-data processing, validation, persistent storage, and secure reporting workflows.

The final result should be a reliable daily operational reporting platform that replaces manual spreadsheet-based dashboard preparation with a structured, verifiable, date-wise digital reporting system.